<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charlotte de La Marck</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1574–1594</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charlotte de La Marck was the heiress of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-la-marck">La Marck family</a>'s principality of Sedan and duchy of Bouillon. In 1591 she married Henri de <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-la-tour-dauvergne">La Tour d'Auvergne</a>, a Protestant ally of Henry IV, and when she died childless in 1594 she left him her lands, which passed to the La Tour d'Auvergne dynasty.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charlotte-de-la-marck.jpg" alt="Charlotte de La Marck" width="320" height="515" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CharlottedelaMarck1570.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
